3. . . . Having fashioned an earth-globe of wood, of the desired size,
4. Fix a staff, passing through the midst of it and protruding at either side, for Meru; and likewise a couple of sustaining hoops (*kakshā*), and the equinoctial hoop;
5. These are to be made with graduated divisions (*angula*) of degrees of the circle (*bhagaṇa*). . . .
